From: Manikanta Mylavarapu <manikanta.mylavarapu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: describe IPQ9574 radio and WSI resources

Enable nodes required for q6 remoteproc bring up.

Describe the IPQ9574-family WLAN register window and named interrupts
observed on the Linksys LN6001. Connect the AHB device to the WCSS remote
processor using the upstream ath11k binding.

Add the IPQ9574 compatible proposed for ath11k support. Describe its
interrupt layout separately from IPQ8074 and IPQ6018: the observed
IPQ9574-family interface omits the watchdog interrupt and provides a fourth
transmit-completion ring. Both layouts contain 52 interrupts.

QCN9274 supports single-PHY and split-PHY configurations. Some fixed split-
PHY designs do not identify that configuration through the OTP board
identifier.

Merged from:
  2013-01-arm64-dts-qcom-ipq9574-add-nodes-to-bring-up-q6.patch
  2013-02-arm64-dts-qcom-ipq9574-add-ath11k-resources.patch
